module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_refused_emission_is_rendered_as_a_poison_string_inside_otherwise_valid_output

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// ONE RULE, NOT ONE ROW PER MARKER. The 22 constants below differ only in which renderer wrote them, so they
// are one failure mode recorded once; a per-module row would make the census count spelling rather than count
// the defect. The row is a candidate set, not a census: it lists what git grep returned at one head, and a site
// is converted when its consumers are touched, not when this list grows.

data a_refused_emission_is_rendered_as_a_poison_string_inside_otherwise_valid_output: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_refused_emission_is_rendered_as_a_poison_string_inside_otherwise_valid_output" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyImpossible,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "each render function returning Outcome of List of String, built with sequence_outcome over its per-statement emissions, so a declined checked builder answers the refusal arm and no marker string can be committed or digested"
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a checked bash builder declines a value, and the renderer that should have failed instead emits an otherwise valid script with a marker line inside it -- a constant such as srv1_bash_emit_refused_poison, whose value is GUNBC-BASH-EMIT-REFUSED, or ci_floor_build_verify_refused_poison at dag/gunbc/ci/ci_spec.dag line 491, whose value is a sentence of prose that is not valid workflow shell. The render is accepted, the digest of the render is a digest of that accepted render, and the only thing that separates it from a good render is a string a consumer would have to know to look for. HARM: a refusal reads as a success at every layer above the emitter -- the generated artifact is committed, a digest of it is recorded as computed on a host, and the script fails only where it runs, which for srv1 is after a boot. The idiom is also a trap for the next consumer: the poison is a String, so any function returning lines can carry it without a type change, and the Optional or Outcome that would have carried the refusal is discarded one call earlier. SPECIMEN: 2026-11-11, review 93554 on PR #16270 at head 014879419d3 -- srv1_replica_container_command_lines and srv1_replica_launcher_lines return List of String, srv1_bash_unwrap turns a declined Optional into a node that prints srv1_bash_emit_refused_poison, and srv1_bash_bare falls back to a literal word when the checked bare-word builder refuses; the reviewer named ci_spec ci_floor_build_verify_script as the same shape. CANDIDATE SET, not a census -- git grep for the token _refused_poison at 014879419d3 returns 22 constants across roughly 30 files, largest concentrations dag/test/claim/host/fleet_keypair_mint_witness.dag 9 sites, dag/gunbc/live_deploy/emit.dag 8, dag/gunbc/shell_command_text.dag 7, dag/gunbc/witness/compiler_gate_contract_stamp.dag 6, src/v2/workflow/gunbc_invoke_step_emit.dag 5, dag/gunbc/ci/ci_spec.dag 4; srv1_serving_replica_layout.dag is NO LONGER in that set -- #16270 converted it, and at this head the module names no constant ending in _refused_poison, no unwrap helper and no builder fallback; by name: bash_emit_program_sequence_refused_poison, bmc_token_smoke_emit_refused_poison, boot_credential_source_emit_refused_poison, ci_floor_build_verify_refused_poison, ci_heal_revalidation_preflight_refused_poison, ci_release_build_refused_poison, ci_retry_emit_refused_poison, ci_sccache_provider_emit_refused_poison, ci_workflow_run_emit_refused_poison, compiler_gate_compose_caller_emit_refused_poison, compiler_gate_contract_stamp_emit_refused_poison, compiler_gate_contract_stamp_evidence_emit_refused_poison, fleet_converge_locked_apply_emit_refused_poison, gunbc_invoke_step_orch_refused_poison, helper_snapshot_readback_emit_refused_poison, live_deploy_effect_materialization_refused_poison, oidc_readback_refused_poison, serve_grammar_refused_poison, shell_command_text_refused_poison, sol_hold_render_refused_poison, witness_emit_refused_poison, and gunbc_invoke_step_emit_refused_poison_prefix. DISTINGUISHING FACT: the poison is a value of the same type as the payload, so the type system cannot separate a refused render from a good one; only a string comparison can, and no consumer performs one. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the marker is chosen so the script fails when it runs rather than silently doing the wrong thing; found while answering review 93554 on PR #16270. REPAIR, per site and never by exception: the render returns the typed shape its neighbouring consumers already use -- Outcome of List of String, or Optional -- assembled with sequence_outcome over the per-statement emissions, so a declined builder, or an Accepted emission that still carries diagnostics, becomes the refusal arm carrying its reason, and there is no marker string left to commit. srv1_serving_replica_layout is the conversion taken in #16270: srv1_bash_emit_refused_poison, srv1_bash_unwrap and the srv1_bash_bare fallback are deleted and both renders answer the typed refusal. CONTROLS: the red for #16270 is in the srv1 boot-path witness and holds at this head -- one_unspellable_config_value_makes_both_renders_refuse_instead_of_rendering_a_marker feeds a config value one checked word builder cannot spell (a container-side TLS directory holding a space: the same input class as the layer below's bash_build_word_var of the name 1x, which bash_fold_bad_var_name_is_refused_holds already pins) and requires BOTH renders to answer the refusal arm naming the refusing site -- the container command directly, and the launcher through the arm whose docker run carries that script -- and an accepted render, even one with no visible marker, fails that control. Every other control in that witness now reads the Accepted arm under an explicit render_answered conjunct, because a control that reads a refusal as an empty list turns a refusal into a passing absence check, which is this defect one level up. CEILING: structurally impossible -- with the render returning Outcome and every consumer forced to match on it, a refused emission has no channel into otherwise valid output: nothing to grep for and nothing to forget to grep for. NEXT TRIGGER: each site converts as that render's consumers are touched, the rule that converted srv1 here; a site is done when its module stops naming any constant ending in _refused_poison.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
